package dbdef

// SceneDao is the scene's own state: the parameters of its time domain
// (gameplay/timedomain). Domain time is a piecewise-linear
// map of business time, D(B) = AnchorDomain + (B − AnchorBusiness) × Rate, and
// these three numbers are the map.
//
// `nopersist,sync`, like a monster's position, and for the same two reasons:
// a scene is rebuilt from configuration on every start (`noPersist=true
// lifetime=runtime_rebuild`), so a 2× set on a dungeon dies with the process;
// and the client needs them — it extrapolates domain time from its own
// estimate of the server's business time with the same formula, which is
// what lets it animate a 2× scene at 2× between frames. Being DAO fields is
// what rolls a refused rate change back.
//
// A scene that must survive a restart (a persistent world with a slowed
// region) declares them persisted instead; the domain then picks up from the
// stored anchor and rate (the framework does not decide that, the tag does).
//
//roost:dao nocoll
type SceneDao struct {
	TimeAnchorBusiness int64   `bson:"time_anchor_business" dao:"nopersist,sync"`
	TimeAnchorDomain   int64   `bson:"time_anchor_domain" dao:"nopersist,sync"`
	TimeRate           float64 `bson:"time_rate" dao:"nopersist,sync"`
}
